/knowledge/tasks/open/task-001-descale.md (Task, state=open)

A task records one piece of work for one person. The text holds no TODO, because the task itself records what remains.

Frontmatter:
  tags (optional): Usually up to 3 values. Never leave out or merge content to stay within the count. When at the limit: Keep the tags that a reader searches for.
    Example:
      tags: [kitchen]
  owner (optional): The owner is the person who does the work.
    Example:
      owner: ada
  state: A task is open while its work remains.
  links (depends-on, optional): A depends-on link points to a task that has to finish first. At most 2 `depends-on` links. Never leave out or merge content to stay within the count. When at the limit: Merge the tasks that this one waits for.
    Example:
      links:
        - rel: depends-on
          to: target-id

# <title>
  The opening says why the work matters.
  prose: The summary says what the work changes. Usually up to 1 paragraph. Never leave out or merge content to stay within the count. When at the limit: Put the details in the steps.

## Steps
  This section lists the steps in order.
  numbered-list: Each step holds one action. A step holds no "then", because each step is one action.

### Notes (absent, optional)
  This section holds what a later step needs to know.
  Example:
    ### Notes

    The vinegar is under the sink.

/knowledge/notes/note-kettle.md (Note)

Preamble:
  The preamble says what the note is about.
  prose: One paragraph introduces the note.

## Details
  bullet-list: Each item names one quirk, with its key before a colon.
    Example:
      - lid: The lid sticks.
